# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Every entry here is something this project actually produces, or a
# costly accident worth guarding against. Boilerplate for toolchains this
# project does not use (packaging builds, Jython, HTML coverage reports)
# was removed deliberately - an ignore rule for a file that can never
# appear only makes the real ones harder to find.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENTS ───
# venv_gpu/ is the documented env (README "Setup"); .venv/ is what
# `uv sync` creates. Never commit either: gigabytes of platform-specific
# binaries that every machine has to build for itself anyway.
venv_gpu/
.venv/

# Not used today, and there are no secrets in this repository (see
# docs/SECURITY.md) - kept because committing one costs far more than this line.
.env

# ─── EVERYTHING THE PROJECT WRITES AS IT RUNS ───
# generated/ (exploration/config.py, GENERATED_DIR): incident evidence
# bundles and clean-run reports (the dashboard), coverage-audit pictures and
# calibration runs (the tools), the training log and TensorBoard curves, the
# power-mode record run_dashboard.bat restores, and the ruff, mypy, pytest
# and coverage caches. Runtime output, not source.
generated/

# ─── PYTHON / TOOL CACHES ───
# Bytecode goes to generated/cache/pycache (tools/pycache_hook.py in the venv,
# common/__init__.py elsewhere), and pyproject.toml sends the ruff, mypy,
# pytest and coverage caches to generated/ too. Only a Python started without
# the hook can still write __pycache__/ next to the source.
__pycache__/
# CI's coverage report (--cov-report=xml), written to the working directory.
coverage.xml

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TRAINING ARTIFACTS  —  the big one
#
# These were previously untracked by accident rather than by design, which
# is how ~90MB of old checkpoint .zip files ended up permanently baked into
# git history across the "Update5/6/7/8" commits. Checkpoints are large
# binaries that change on every run and are already managed by
# train_agent.py, not by git.
#
# The 6M brain (mario_brain_checkpoint.zip, Objective 1) is NOT tracked any
# more (2026-09-29): a clone ships the final 16M brain instead (THE MAIN
# BRAIN, below). The 6M file stays in git history and in artifacts.json; get
# it back with `git checkout b27e9d2 -- mario_brain_checkpoint.zip`.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
checkpoints/
mario_brain_*checkpoint*.zip

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EXPLORATION / QA ARTIFACTS
# exploration_data/ generated masks, jump arcs and bootstrap coverage
# checkpoints_qa/   the QA-phase model zips + their paired coverage, and
#                   final_objective2_16000000/ - the Objective-2 closure
#                   record and its evidence
#                   (their SHA-256s ARE tracked, in artifacts.json)
# EXCEPTION: the two files the dashboard needs to run the final 16M brain
# ARE tracked - the approval record it checks the brain against, and the
# reachable-space mask its coverage map is measured on. git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, hence `dir/*`.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
exploration_data/*
!exploration_data/reachable_mask.npz
checkpoints_qa/*
!checkpoints_qa/final_objective2_16000000/
checkpoints_qa/final_objective2_16000000/*
!checkpoints_qa/final_objective2_16000000/FINAL_OBJECTIVE2.json

# Completion-test results, one per evaluated brain (tools/evaluate_completion.py
# and verify_level1.py); the 16M brain's is hash-protected and read when
# choosing what to resume, so it stays beside the evaluation code.
# evaluation/completion_baseline_6M.json sits OUTSIDE results/ on purpose: it
# is the frozen baseline, tracked and hash-protected, not a run output.
evaluation/results/

# Release assets built by `python tools/final_brain.py bundle` (the final
# 16M brain bundle is published as a GitHub Release asset, never committed).
dist/

# The QA-phase master lives at the repo root, next to (never on top of)
# mario_brain_checkpoint.zip. It is NOT tracked: training overwrites it, and
# each push would add a new 20MB blob to history.
glitch_hunter_qa.zip
glitch_hunter_qa_coverage.npz

# THE MAIN BRAIN: the approved 16,000,000-step Objective-2 brain and its
# coverage map (glitch_hunter_main_brain.zip, glitch_hunter_main_brain_coverage.npz)
# ARE tracked since 2026-09-29, so a fresh clone plays the final brain with no
# download. It is frozen: do NOT re-commit a retrained brain over it. Its
# SHA-256s are in artifacts.json.

# ─── EDITORS & OS ───
# What the common editors and the Windows and macOS file managers drop into
# a folder (CONTRIBUTING.md invites contributors).
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NOT IGNORED, ON PURPOSE - listed here so nobody "helpfully" adds them:
#   uv.lock                     - the lockfile; committing it is what makes
#                                 `uv sync` reproducible for your friend.
#   dashboard/web/static/vendor/          - the vendored socket.io client. It is a
#                                 dependency we deliberately ship so the
#                                 dashboard works with no internet.
#   glitch_hunter_main_brain.zip, glitch_hunter_main_brain_coverage.npz,
#   checkpoints_qa/final_objective2_16000000/FINAL_OBJECTIVE2.json,
#   exploration_data/reachable_mask.npz - the final 16M brain; see above.
#   artifacts.json              - the SHA-256 of every protected artifact,
#                                 including ones that are themselves ignored.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
